# Leaving the battlefield is losing control of it (Khârn the Betrayer's and Gustha's Scepter's rulings). Bot1 takes Bot2's
# Skullclamp onto its Grizzly Bears, and Bot2 destroys the Skullclamp with Shatter: "when you lose control of that
# Equipment this turn" triggers, its "if" true as the Skullclamp left attached to Bot1's Bears; on resolution the
# Skullclamp is gone (CR 603.4, 400.7), so the trigger does nothing.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Grizzly Bears
Stolen Uniform
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Skullclamp
Shatter
Mountain x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Grizzly Bears.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Skullclamp.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Stolen Uniform.Cast
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Skullclamp)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears.Toughness = 1
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Shatter.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Skullclamp)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Stack.Count = 0
? Bot1.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears.Toughness = 2

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Sapphire; Mox Emerald; Mox Pearl; Grizzly Bears
Bot2.Graveyard = Shatter; Skullclamp
